WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:12.180
Messier 7 or M7, also designated NGC 6475 and sometimes known as Ptolemy's Cluster, is an open cluster of stars in the constellation of Scorpius.

00:12.717 --> 00:18.159
The cluster is easily detectable with the naked eye, close to the "stinger" of Scorpius.

00:18.704 --> 00:24.601
With a declination of −34.8°, it is the southernmost Messier object.
